/var/home/dylan/projects/disclaude/docs/WORK-ORDERS-archive.md:117:- [x] **BW-01 (MERGED 58b37c7) — Build can't send a SECOND plan/revision.** ROOT CAUSE CONFIRMED (trace `conv_2907c89b`, repeated 5x): the actionless valve FORCE-FINISHES the re-plan. After 3 tool-less turns (`_ACTIONLESS_BREAK_CAP`, engine.py:548) during a re-plan, `Valve.actionless_valve` (turn_control.py:181-197) runs the done-build finish guard; `signals.plan_steps_complete` reads the LATEST PlanEvent = the still-done revision-1 (rev-2 never submitted) + `productive_actions_since_approval>0`, so it emits `FINISHED(completed_via_notify)` and yanks the user out of PLANNING. ENGINE bug (request DID reach the loop — status detail=planning at seq 93). FIX: suppress the completed_via_notify finish branch when in-planning-for-a-revision (latest `planning` seq > latest `plan_approved` seq — engine.py:1072-1076 already computes this; factor into a signals helper `in_planning_for_revision`), fall through to the plan-nudge instead. Model-behavior aggravator (prose-only turns) is secondary; the defect is finishing AT ALL during a pending re-plan.
